    "number": 36619,
    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "rest: don't log an error for /spenttxouts on a block without undo data",
    "user": {
      "login": "kriss39",
      "id": 93033289,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBYuTSQ",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93033289?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/kriss39",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kriss39/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`/rest/spenttxouts/<hash>` reads the undo file for every block above genesis. For a block that was stored but never connected (a side branch) or whose undo data was pruned, there is no undo position, so `OpenUndoFile()` fails and `ReadBlockUndo()` writes `OpenUndoFile failed for FlatFilePos(nFile=-1, nPos=0)` to debug.log with `LogError`. The request itself already returns 404, but each unauthenticated request for such a block adds an `[error]` line that looks like disk corruption.\r\n\r\nThis checks `BLOCK_HAVE_UNDO` and `IsBlockPruned()` before reading, the same way `getblock` does, so nothing is logged. The response is unchanged.\r\n\r\nThe new check at the end of `interface_rest.py` requests a stale block and fails on master because of the logged error.\r\n",
